        <h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>
        <p><strong>Which propellant is safest for aerosols?</strong><br />
        Nitrogen, carbon dioxide, and compressed air are the safest from a flammability and toxicity standpoint.</p>

        <p><strong>Is LPG legally allowed for aerosols in India?</strong><br />
        Yes, LPG is permitted under controlled manufacture, storage, and transport regulations governed by PESO and related safety authorities.</p>

        <p><strong>Can DME fully replace LPG?</strong><br />
        DME can replace LPG in many water-based and personal care products but not universally across all industrial applications.</p>

        <p><strong>Which propellant is most eco-friendly?</strong><br />
        Nitrogen, carbon dioxide, and compressed air do not contribute to ozone depletion or significant global warming.</p>

        <p><strong>Which propellant is best for export products?</strong><br />
        Export compliance depends on the target country regulations, but compressed gases and low-GWP propellants are generally preferred.</p>

